OL,3,AGrid operator says lights will stay on
OL,4,Athis winter after concerns
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe body in charge of Britain's
OL,7,Felectricity network has given
OL,8,Fassurances that the lights will stay on
OL,9,Fthis winter after concerns were raised
OL,10,Fby some of its engineers.
OL,12,FThe National Energy System Operator
OL,13,F(NESO) said the country's electricity
OL,14,Fsystem was prepared and "resilient to
OL,15,Fthe challenges it may face" during the
OL,16,Fcolder months.
OL,23,APub: 22-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,305,300,200,140,0,100
PN,11908
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F119A1792731297
OL,1,W5j 5Q7kjs15j 5ws
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AGrid operator says lights will stay on
OL,4,Athis winter after concerns
OL,5,
OL,6,FHowever, its winter outlook report
OL,7,Fcomes after an independent
OL,8,Finvestigation found engineers had "high
OL,9,Flevels of stress and concern" about
OL,10,Ftheir ability to ensure adequate supply
OL,11,Fdue to differences between renewable
OL,12,Fand gas-fired power generation.
OL,14,FNESO said supplies were expected to
OL,15,Fremain secure throughout the winter,
OL,16,Fthough warned there could be "tight
OL,17,Fdays".
OL,23,APub: 22-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG8/39
